WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:07.210
A station is any point you take readings at — an
open well, a bore, a check dam, a rain gauge.

00:07.330 --> 00:11.746
This tutorial is about the My stations page,
where you keep them.

00:12.550 --> 00:15.310
Now we're on: My stations.

00:15.430 --> 00:21.310
This page is your notebook of water sources —
every well, gauge and dam you look after,

00:21.430 --> 00:24.286
each with its latest reading and status.

00:24.406 --> 00:30.070
Right now it shows Asha's practice stations;
your own list will grow just like this.

00:30.883 --> 00:32.683
Add a new station.

00:32.803 --> 00:39.979
Every water source you monitor is a station — a
well, borehole, rain gauge, check-dam and so on.

00:40.099 --> 00:46.459
Tap here to register a new one: give it a name,
location and type, and it joins your list.

00:47.283 --> 00:49.155
Find and filter.

00:49.275 --> 00:54.219
As your list grows, search by station name,
code or village here.

00:54.339 --> 01:00.219
Open the filters to show just one station type, or
only the stations that are due for a measurement.

01:01.050 --> 01:02.682
Open a station.

01:02.802 --> 01:06.306
Each station shows its latest reading and
status.

01:06.426 --> 01:13.530
Tap one to open its full details, photos and history
— and from there you can record a reading, edit it,

01:13.650 --> 01:15.498
or show it on the map.

01:16.317 --> 01:18.261
That is the whole page.

01:18.381 --> 01:23.037
You can replay this tutorial any time from the
Learning page inside the app.

01:23.157 --> 01:25.821
Thanks for helping look after our water.
